# Ported from Fortune13 / LoneStar / desertrose-1 (SS13) — Misfits Add

ent-N14WeaponSMGPPSh41 = PPSh-41
    .desc = A Soviet-era submachine gun firing 9mm from a 35-round drum at a terrifying rate of fire. Crude and reliable in equal measure — scavengers prize it for its simplicity and ease of maintenance.

ent-N14WeaponSMG9mm = .45 Auto SMG
    .desc = A pre-war .45 Auto submachine gun with a detachable magazine and a threaded muzzle for a suppressor.

ent-N14WeaponSMG10mmSuppressed = Sleepytyme
    .desc = A unique, permanently suppressed 10mm submachine gun. Quiet, compact, and built for work after dark.

ent-N14WeaponSMGAmerican180 = American 180
    .desc = A .22 LR submachine gun fed by a 35-round drum with an integrated suppressor. Whisper-quiet and ferociously fast. What it lacks in stopping power it more than compensates for in round volume.

ent-N14MagazineSMG9mmDrum = smg drum magazine (9mm)
    .desc = A 71-round drum magazine loaded with 9mm Parabellum cartridges. Compatible with the PPSh-41.

ent-N14MagazineAmerican180Drum = smg drum magazine (.22lr)
    .desc = A 177-round drum magazine loaded with .22 Long Rifle cartridges. Fits the American 180 submachine gun.
